 60NI c  Measured |b-asymmetry parameter by polarizing the {+60}Co source       
 60NI2c  by low-temperature nuclear orientation method. The source was cooled   
 60NI3c  to milliKelvin in a {+3}He-{+4}He dilution refrigerator in an external 
 60NI4c  magnetic field of 13 Tesla. Measured |b-particle spectra using         
 60NI5c  a Si PIn diode operating at 10K in a magnetic field of 0.6 Tesla.      
 60NI6c  Gamma rays were detected with an HPGe detector placed outside the      
 60NI7c  refrigerator. The |b{+-} data were taken at cold and warm              
 60NI8c  temperatures at angles of 0|' and 90|'. For analysis, only the         
 60NI9c  upper half of the |b spectrum was used. Monte Carlo simulations.       
 60NI c  Level scheme data are from {+60}Co to {+60}Ni decay dataset in         
 60NI2c  ENSDF database, with rounded values of energies and intensities        
